WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:03.302
-Hey, everybody,
let's step over to the desk.

00:00:03.302 --> 00:00:13.312
♪♪

00:00:13.312 --> 00:00:20.420
♪♪

00:00:20.420 --> 00:00:21.855
Uh...

00:00:21.855 --> 00:00:23.923
[ Laughter ]

00:00:23.923 --> 00:00:25.692
-That made you tired.
-It's the end of the we--

00:00:25.692 --> 00:00:28.294
[ Laughter ]

00:00:28.294 --> 00:00:32.398
-I felt how heavy that window
was on my fake space work.

00:00:32.398 --> 00:00:35.568
It is the --
[ Laughter ]

00:00:35.568 --> 00:00:36.902
There's no water
allowed on the set.

00:00:36.902 --> 00:00:38.604
There's a lot of things.

00:00:38.604 --> 00:00:39.939
It's the end of the week,
and that's usually

00:00:39.939 --> 00:00:41.507
when I catch up
on some personal stuff.

00:00:41.507 --> 00:00:43.609
I check my inbox,
return some e-mails,

00:00:43.609 --> 00:00:45.578
and, of course,
I send out thank-you notes.

00:00:45.578 --> 00:00:47.046
Well, I was running a bit behind
today so I thought

00:00:47.046 --> 00:00:48.581
if you guys wouldn't mind,
I'd like to write out

00:00:48.581 --> 00:00:49.849
my weekly thank-you notes
right now.

00:00:49.849 --> 00:00:51.617
Is that cool with you guys?
I hope so.

00:00:51.617 --> 00:00:53.153
[ Applause ]
James --

00:00:53.153 --> 00:00:54.820
I haven't said this
in a long time.

00:00:54.820 --> 00:00:56.956
James, can I get some
thank-you-note-writing music?

00:00:56.956 --> 00:01:00.092
♪♪

00:01:00.092 --> 00:01:01.227
Wow.

00:01:01.227 --> 00:01:02.595
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:02.595 --> 00:01:04.129
Wow.

00:01:04.129 --> 00:01:06.065
Oh, my -- Oh!
Oh. Oh, my God.

00:01:06.065 --> 00:01:08.701
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:08.701 --> 00:01:09.769
Wait, wait, wait.

00:01:09.769 --> 00:01:11.771
You were playing that
with one hand?

00:01:11.771 --> 00:01:12.771
♪♪

00:01:12.771 --> 00:01:13.906
There you go, perfect.

00:01:13.906 --> 00:01:16.776
Mm.

00:01:16.776 --> 00:01:18.244
♪♪

00:01:18.244 --> 00:01:22.481
Thank you, viral video of cakes
that don't look like cakes

00:01:22.481 --> 00:01:24.583
for being the reason why the
President spent the morning

00:01:24.583 --> 00:01:26.919
trying to cut his stapler
with a fork.

00:01:26.919 --> 00:01:28.455
[ Light laughter ]

00:01:31.191 --> 00:01:32.791
We're gonna have
to speed these up a little bit

00:01:32.791 --> 00:01:35.228
with all the --
[ Clears throat ] -- dead air.

00:01:35.228 --> 00:01:37.863
[ Laughter ]

00:01:37.863 --> 00:01:39.332
Hoo.

00:01:39.332 --> 00:01:42.068
-Not if you do that little dance
move after each thank-you note.

00:01:42.068 --> 00:01:44.103
-After each thank-you, you want
me to do which dance move?

00:01:44.103 --> 00:01:46.339
-Help me pick one.

00:01:46.339 --> 00:01:54.847
♪♪

00:01:54.847 --> 00:01:56.081
[ Laughter ]

00:01:56.081 --> 00:01:59.185
-I ate your -- [ Laughs ]
I ate your head, and...

00:01:59.185 --> 00:02:01.954
-Yeah, we saw.

00:02:01.954 --> 00:02:03.490
-Swallowed it.

00:02:03.490 --> 00:02:06.159
Changed your hairstyle,
regurgitated it.

00:02:06.159 --> 00:02:07.660
[ Laughter ]

00:02:07.660 --> 00:02:09.162
♪♪

00:02:09.162 --> 00:02:11.064
Thank you, Ivanka Trump

00:02:11.064 --> 00:02:14.400
telling unemployed Americans
to "find something new,"

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:16.735
for sounding less like
an economic recovery plan

00:02:16.735 --> 00:02:18.871
and more like something
you'd find stitched on a pillow

00:02:18.871 --> 00:02:20.673
at a beach house.

00:02:20.673 --> 00:02:22.742
"Find something new."
Maybe I will find something new.

00:02:26.546 --> 00:02:28.414
[ Laughter ]

00:02:28.414 --> 00:02:30.717
-Why do you keep slamming it?

00:02:30.717 --> 00:02:33.986
[ Laughter ]

00:02:33.986 --> 00:02:36.856
-Am I hitting it down?
-That was loud.

00:02:36.856 --> 00:02:38.958
-All right,
I'll do it in silence.

00:02:38.958 --> 00:02:40.459
♪♪

00:02:40.459 --> 00:02:44.129
Thank you, study that says dogs
experience separation anxiety

00:02:44.129 --> 00:02:46.332
when their owners
return to work,

00:02:46.332 --> 00:02:48.768
while cats are just like,
"Bye-bye, bish."

00:02:48.768 --> 00:02:50.470
[ Light laughter ]

00:02:54.140 --> 00:02:56.642
[ Laughter ]

00:02:56.642 --> 00:02:59.946
I think it sounded
a little tappy over there.

00:02:59.946 --> 00:03:01.380
♪♪

00:03:01.380 --> 00:03:03.415
Thank you, face masks,

00:03:03.415 --> 00:03:06.185
for being the new fuzzy dice
in everyone's car.

00:03:06.185 --> 00:03:09.222
[ Laughter ]

00:03:14.193 --> 00:03:15.194
♪♪

00:03:15.194 --> 00:03:18.063
[ Laughter ]

00:03:18.063 --> 00:03:21.534
Oh, man.
I don't know.

00:03:21.534 --> 00:03:22.802
♪♪

00:03:22.802 --> 00:03:25.404
Thank you, new avocado milk,

00:03:25.404 --> 00:03:28.641
for being green while also being
the whitest thing ever.

00:03:28.641 --> 00:03:31.944
[ Light laughter ]

00:03:31.944 --> 00:03:35.815
"Um, pardon me.
Do you have avocado milk?"

00:03:38.718 --> 00:03:40.720
Oh, here's another one.
A double dip.

00:03:40.720 --> 00:03:41.721
-Hmm.

00:03:41.721 --> 00:03:43.055
♪♪

00:03:43.055 --> 00:03:44.791
Thank you, avocado milk.

00:03:44.791 --> 00:03:47.827
[ Laughter ]

00:03:47.827 --> 00:03:48.861
-That's it.

00:03:48.861 --> 00:03:51.097
[ Laughter ]

00:03:51.097 --> 00:03:53.666
I'm the new spokesman
for avocado milk.

00:03:53.666 --> 00:03:56.402
Thank you, avocado milk.

00:03:56.402 --> 00:03:58.671
[ Laughter ]

00:03:58.671 --> 00:04:00.706
-That's a thing?
-Oh, yeah, man.

00:04:00.706 --> 00:04:02.675
This is it.
It's like the new oatmeal.

00:04:02.675 --> 00:04:05.444
-Oh. Okay.
[ Laughs ]

00:04:05.444 --> 00:04:06.511
♪♪

00:04:06.511 --> 00:04:08.815
-Thank you, avocado milk.

00:04:08.815 --> 00:04:11.884
Sure, you're really expensive,
but at least you taste terrible.

00:04:11.884 --> 00:04:15.688
[ Laughter ]

00:04:17.256 --> 00:04:19.091
Oh, my goodness.

00:04:19.091 --> 00:04:22.194
Triple dip?
-Three avocados?

00:04:22.194 --> 00:04:24.497
-It's three-layer
avocado milk day.

00:04:24.497 --> 00:04:26.599
-Yes, yes, let's have it,
let's have it.

00:04:26.599 --> 00:04:28.433
-You ready?
-Yeah, let's do it.

00:04:28.433 --> 00:04:31.404
-We've never done this
when we did the regular show.

00:04:31.404 --> 00:04:32.405
-Three in a row.

00:04:32.405 --> 00:04:35.307
-Here we go, man.
[ Chuckles ]

00:04:35.307 --> 00:04:36.642
♪♪

00:04:36.642 --> 00:04:38.377
Thank you, avocado milk...

00:04:38.377 --> 00:04:40.913
[ Laughter ]

00:04:40.913 --> 00:04:43.048
...for letting me fulfill
my longtime fantasy

00:04:43.048 --> 00:04:44.483
of drinking Baby Yoda.

00:04:44.483 --> 00:04:48.187
[ Laughter ]
Oh, hey! Come on, hey!

00:04:48.187 --> 00:04:50.122
Not tonight, kids.
Time to go to bed.

00:04:50.122 --> 00:04:51.491
Come on.

00:04:51.491 --> 00:04:53.526
Not tonight.

00:04:55.161 --> 00:04:56.528
No.
-Yeah, come on.

00:04:56.528 --> 00:04:58.264
No, there isn't.
This is a regular one.

00:04:58.264 --> 00:05:00.132
-There's got to be more.
-Nope.

00:05:00.132 --> 00:05:01.601
-You got to freestyle one.

00:05:01.601 --> 00:05:05.237
[ Laughter ]

00:05:05.237 --> 00:05:07.106
-Oh, gosh.
Uh...

00:05:07.106 --> 00:05:13.512
Oh, gosh.
Um...uh, uh...

00:05:13.512 --> 00:05:15.281
♪♪

00:05:15.281 --> 00:05:16.281
[ Laughter ]

00:05:16.281 --> 00:05:18.084
-You're not even doing it?

00:05:18.084 --> 00:05:19.519
You don't have
to freestyle that.

00:05:19.519 --> 00:05:21.487
[ Laughter ]

00:05:21.487 --> 00:05:23.856
-You always play the same song.

00:05:23.856 --> 00:05:27.226
You're gonna freestyle, too?

00:05:27.226 --> 00:05:30.429
I've got --
Uh, uh...

00:05:30.429 --> 00:05:32.431
Gosh, just give me two seconds.

00:05:32.431 --> 00:05:34.133
Can we do
a "Please stand by" thing?

00:05:34.133 --> 00:05:40.573
♪♪

00:05:40.573 --> 00:05:42.375
-Let this be the whole show.

00:05:42.375 --> 00:05:43.375
[ Laughter ]

00:05:43.375 --> 00:05:47.747
-I got it.

00:05:47.747 --> 00:05:49.014
♪♪

00:05:49.014 --> 00:05:52.318
-Thank you, avocado milk.

00:05:52.318 --> 00:05:55.154
When I poured you
in my coffee the first time,

00:05:55.154 --> 00:05:56.989
I was like, "Holy guacamole."

00:05:56.989 --> 00:05:59.592
[ Laughter ]
[ Bell dings ]

00:05:59.592 --> 00:06:02.261
-All right.
You did it, you did it.

00:06:02.261 --> 00:06:04.630
♪♪

00:06:04.630 --> 00:06:07.400
-James Fallon,
ladies and gentlemen.

00:06:07.400 --> 00:06:08.634
Come on, give it up,
give it up.

00:06:08.634 --> 00:06:10.536
-No, man.
-Give it up.

00:06:10.536 --> 00:06:12.171
[ Applause ]

00:06:12.171 --> 00:06:13.639
-Awful joke.

00:06:13.639 --> 00:06:14.907
That's why we have writers.

00:06:14.907 --> 00:06:19.245
That's why we have writers
and the whole -- oh, man.

00:06:19.245 --> 00:06:20.579
♪♪

00:06:20.579 --> 00:06:24.250
Thank you, texts that start with
"Sorry, just saw this,"

00:06:24.250 --> 00:06:25.752
for being a fun way of saying,

00:06:25.752 --> 00:06:27.486
"Hey, you like
being lied to, right?"

00:06:27.486 --> 00:06:30.323
[ Laughter ]

00:06:30.323 --> 00:06:33.459
-Oh, man.

00:06:33.459 --> 00:06:36.028
That's me all day.
-"Yeah, this oughta be..."

00:06:36.028 --> 00:06:38.164
-I'm just gonna start saying,
"Hey, you like being lied to?"

00:06:38.164 --> 00:06:40.966
-Yeah, yeah, people get it.
Might as well.

00:06:40.966 --> 00:06:42.902
Here's the last one.
Here we go.

00:06:42.902 --> 00:06:44.202
♪♪

00:06:44.202 --> 00:06:46.105
Thank you, Kanye West,

00:06:46.105 --> 00:06:49.041
for launching the Quibi
of presidential campaigns.

00:06:49.041 --> 00:06:50.042
There you have it, everybody.

00:06:50.042 --> 00:06:51.244
Those are our "Thank You Notes."

